WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.670
Some of these stories are so unbelievable,
unbelievable that they actually do seem like

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.820
they're not real, except they are.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:07.820
And I've

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.850
talked about the problem with calling them
unbelievable because it actually creates a

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:15.350
sort of disbelief of things that are all too
real and should horrify us.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.100
And this is going to be sort of a short story
since it's still developing.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.840
I did want to briefly cover it.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:25.910
A top Trump national security advisor has
been reportedly escorted out of the white

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:32.450
house and placed on leave when it was uncovered
that they were potentially a security risk.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:36.660
Remember we were told Donald Trump can be
trusted to hire the right people, that you

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.030
can be trusted with sensitive information,
with information security, all of that stuff.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:45.480
Hillary couldn't be trusted except then Trump
is spilling secrets to Russian spy recruiters

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.950
in the oval office using unsecured, uh, devices
that he refuses to have screened.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.980
And here appears to have someone who's a security
risk working in the white house.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.570
I'm talking about a guy named Andrew peek.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:02.690
Andrew peek is or was the senior director
for European and Russian affairs at the national

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.040
security council.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.499
This is like one of Trump's top Russia advisors.

00:01:07.499 --> 00:01:11.149
He is now on leave and a security investigation
is taking place.

00:01:11.149 --> 00:01:16.340
Trump had someone on the national security
council previously at the state department,

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:23.039
his top person on Russia involved in all sorts
of sensitive areas and that guy had to be

00:01:23.039 --> 00:01:26.430
escorted out of the white house by security.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:27.869
The white house was asked for comment.

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:32.399
They said, we don't discuss security matters,
which of course confirms that this is a security

00:01:32.399 --> 00:01:33.399
matter.

00:01:33.399 --> 00:01:36.600
A peek himself was asked to comment, said,
no comment.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:42.159
So it's not just that Donald Trump is hiring
bad people, he's hiring people who are potentially

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:47.169
security threats that security has to escort
out.

00:01:47.169 --> 00:01:52.989
But the bigger picture issue is that this
is the third time in a year that this position

00:01:52.989 --> 00:01:53.989
is vacant.

00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:58.429
Nevermind other positions of importance, and
someone sent me a funny message because peak

00:01:58.429 --> 00:02:00.289
advises Trump on Russia stuff.

00:02:00.289 --> 00:02:04.759
I got an email that said, Hey David, do you
think peak was escorted out because it was

00:02:04.759 --> 00:02:08.829
revealed he's in cahoots with Putin or do
you think he was escorted out because it was

00:02:08.829 --> 00:02:12.530
revealed that he's not in cahoots with Putin
and that doesn't work for Donald Trump?

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.390
Very clever at this point.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:15.819
It's all speculation.

00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:20.799
I actually think that the entire security
threat story might be false.

00:02:20.799 --> 00:02:22.530
And I'll explain what I mean by that.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.110
Andrew peek was an intelligence officer for
a long time.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.830
He has a doctorate in international affairs.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:33.720
He was appointed, I believe, by David Petraeus
under the Barack Obama administration.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:40.180
It's possible that Trump missed this guy in
the firings of Obama people.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.430
And now after the Iranian fat fiasco, it's
possible.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:47.190
Peek started speaking out saying what you're
doing is crazy.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.859
And then it was realized by the Trump administration.

00:02:49.859 --> 00:02:52.370
Oh damn, how did this guy slip through the
cracks?

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:56.730
He's got to go, let's escort him out and say
that there's a security investigation going

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:57.730
on.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:02:58.909
I, it's mere speculation.

00:02:58.909 --> 00:03:00.090
It's all crazy.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:03.760
I don't know what the final resolution would
be, but remember it was Trump who said, I

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:05.189
will hire the best people.

00:03:05.189 --> 00:03:07.939
It was Trump who said, the people around me
are just going to be the best.

00:03:07.939 --> 00:03:15.209
And, uh, you know, that if you want proof
that Trumpists were bamboozled by that line,

00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:19.840
think back to someone else who tried to use
that same bullet point and was excoriated

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:26.120
Herman Cain, Herman Cain is this pizza entrepreneur
who ran for president, uh, for the Republican

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.120
nomination.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.831
I want to say it was 2012 although maybe it
was in 2008.

00:03:29.831 --> 00:03:32.250
And can you imagine if that was 12 years ago?

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.569
It feels so recent.

00:03:33.569 --> 00:03:37.959
Anyway, Herman Cain ran for the Republican
nomination and one of the things that Herman

00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:41.730
Cain started saying early on when he was asked
about what would your policy be in Afghanistan,

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:46.099
or you know, people were asking policy, uh,
heavy questions.

00:03:46.099 --> 00:03:49.499
He would say, haven't figured it out yet,
but I'm going to put the best person in charge

00:03:49.499 --> 00:03:51.450
of figuring that out.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:56.400
And maybe his followers sort of bought it,
but the Republican party at large did not

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:01.060
buy it and he was completely laughed at and
his campaign fell apart relative relatively

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:02.999
quick, quickly after he said that.

00:04:02.999 --> 00:04:06.799
On the other hand, you've had Donald Trump
effectively saying the same thing, which is

00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:11.510
that Donald Trump did a better job of pretending
to know about stuff like trade and healthcare

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:12.739
or whatever.

00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:17.030
But he also pushed a lot of the same idea
that he was going to hire the best people.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:19.829
He was going to drain the swamp and put the
best people in.

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:23.949
It's really the same failed idea that Herman
Cain put forward about.

00:04:23.949 --> 00:04:28.389
I'll figure it out when I get there and I'll
put people in place who are going to know,

00:04:28.389 --> 00:04:32.340
but with Donald Trump at work than it actually
succeeded at bamboozling enough of his followers

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:37.240
and even enough Republicans who said, I trust
that Donald Trump is going to take our advice.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:40.810
And Trump sometimes alluded to that by saying,
Hey, you know what?

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:47.220
Uh, I will select justices to the Supreme
court from a list given to me by, I think

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.900
it was the heritage foundation.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:54.950
I will select judges for lower court levels
from lists that are generated by this group

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:55.950
or that group.

00:04:55.950 --> 00:05:00.430
So Trump was equally clueless about a lot
of these policy issues, but he played the

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:03.020
game about hiring the right people.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:06.560
Of course, it was a complete and total farce
and he didn't do that in a whole bunch of

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:11.470
his people have been indicted, if not forced
out for different reasons, many of them internationally

00:05:11.470 --> 00:06:52.090
embarrassing.

